      "writtenOn": "2018-12-21T21:29:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with Diasuke that the overload of state containing enable/lock bits and waiter ID bits makes this code hard to follow.  \n\nI would like to see wrapper functions around update_reset_state() that have a descriptive name of the actual action being performed.\n\nThis call here could be something like unlock_resets() or enable_resets().  This would return true only if waiters is zero.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 566,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 566,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "e33610a741d6fccee39d7689b06355d534bbc14e",
