      "writtenOn": "2018-12-21T21:29:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Under what conditions \"with correctly written code\" could task_disable_resets() be called and have either TASK_RESET_LOCK set or have bits set in TASK_WAITERS_MASK?  The only other place TASK_RESET_LOCK is set is in task_reset().  If task_reset() sets the lock, then the task is reset immediately.\n\nI think the sleep forever may be unneeded here, and it would be better to add two asserts:\n\nASSERT((*state \u0026 TASK_RESET_STATE_MASK) \u003d\u003d TASK_RESET_STATE_UNLOCKED)\nASSERT((*state \u0026 TASK_WAITERS_MASK) \u003d\u003d 0)\n\nAlternatively, if update_reset_state() fails, then ASSERT.",
      "range": {
